---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="recur">
  <article class="project-page">

    <header class="project-header">
      <h1>recur</h1>
      <div class="project-meta mono muted">
        <span>2026</span>
        <span>cli / python / local-first</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/cabi-net/recur" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github ↗</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="project-body">

      <p>recur is a minimal command-line journal that surfaces echoes between past and present entries. write a thought; if a word you used has appeared before, recur finds that older entry and brings it forward. you can leave it or rewrite it. either way, the new entry is saved.</p>

      <p>entries are stored locally at <span class="mono">~/.recur/entries.json</span> . the resonance is accidental and slightly random by design: the same entry won't always surface the same memory.</p>

      <!-- <img src="/assets/recur-demo.gif" alt="recur running in a terminal" /> -->

      <a href="https://github.com/cabi-net/recur" class="repo-link mono">→ view repository</a>

    </section>

  </article>
</Base>

<style>
.project-page { max-width: 720px; }

.project-header { margin-bottom: var(--space-xl); }

h1 {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: var(--size-3xl);
  font-weight: normal;
  margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
}

.project-meta {
  display: flex;
  gap: var(--space-lg);
  font-size: var(--size-xs);
}

.project-body p {
  max-width: 65ch;
  line-height: 1.8;
}

.project-body p + p { margin-top: var(--space-lg); }

.project-body img,
.project-body iframe {
  margin: var(--space-xl) 0;
  width: 100%;
}

.repo-link {
  display: inline-block;
  margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  font-size: var(--size-sm);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  padding-bottom: 2px;
}
</style>